      <div type="clause" n="9">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 9</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>De<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.6"/> la were primereinement rendrad l’om de l’hamsochne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.b"/> a la vedve e as orfenins X sol.; e le surplus les parenz e les orfenins partent entre eus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.21"/><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>De la were primerament rendrat l’um de hal[sf]anc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.22"/> a la vedve<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.23"/> e as orphanins X solz; e le surplus les<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.24"/> orphanins e les parenz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.25"/> departent entr’ els.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>[9] Quid fiat de were. De were ergo pro occiso soluto primo uidue X sol. dentur, et residuum liberi et consanguinei inter se diuidant.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="9" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="256" ed="#robertson"/>De la were primereinement rendrad l'om de l'[halsfang] a la vedve e as orfenins X sol., e le surplus les parenz e les orfenins partent entre eus.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>9. Von dem Wergeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.de.1"/> soll man zuerst an Halsfang<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_9.lnote.de.2"/> der Wittwe und den Waisen 10 Schill. geben; und das Übrige theilen die Verwandten und die Waisen unter sich.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">9. Of the wergild one shall first give 10 shill. as healsfang to the widow and the orphans; and the remainder the kinsmen and the orphans divide among themselves.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="257" ed="#robertson"/>As the first instalment of the wergeld 10 shillings shall be paid as healsfang to the widow and orphans, and the relatives and the orphans shall divide what remains among themselves.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 256–257 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 498–499, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De la w. <hi rend="italic">nimmt als Rubrik MAT.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">De la w. taken as a rubric by MAT.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> halsfang <hi rend="italic">aus I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read halsfang from I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">IX. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">IX. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">halt sanc [sainc <hi rend="italic">Io</hi>] <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">halt sanc [sainc Io] I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">vid. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">vid. Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">parens <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">parens Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">287</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Sippe 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Sippe 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_9.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">287</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Halsfang 2b. 5b. Zur Verderbnis des Terminus <hi rend="italic">ebd</hi>. 1. Laut L empfängt die Witwe (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 5) allein den Halsfang: entweder durch Auslassungsfehler; oder sie ist Vertreterin des Nachlasses, wie auch sonst; <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. eheliches Güterrecht 3h. i</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Halsfang 2b. 5b. On the corruption of the term <hi rend="italic">ibid</hi>. 1. According to L the widow (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 5) alone receives the halsfang: either through an error of omission; or she is the representative of the estate, as elsewhere too; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> eheliches Güterrecht 3h. i</seg></note>
      </div>
